  "lines": {
    "prologue": {
      "Hold the road.": "command",
      "That is how the songs tell it.": "dread",
      "Two thousand years ago there were seven kingdoms: six in a ring, each with its own magic, and Orrun in the middle, where all their roads met.": "calm",
      "The songs say Orrun's king, Vael-Orrun, wanted all six crowns.": "calm",
      "He learned a power that makes magic stop.": "dread",
      "Where his armies walked, fire would not burn.": "dread",
      "The six monarchs beat him.": "pride",
      "They drove him and his army down the Rift, a chasm miles deep, and shut them behind the Black Gate at the bottom.": "passion",
      "They made its key from his crown: the Heartstone.": "calm",
      "Then they gave their lives to keep the Gate shut.": "grief",
      "Their spirits sleep in their lands.": "awe",
      "We call them the Wardens.": "pride",
      "On his ruins we built Solenne, my city, with the Heartstone at its heart and the Sunstone above it, a lens whose light the things of the dark cannot bear.": "pride",
      "Six years ago, my Lord Marshal, Cassivane, lost his daughter Ilyra in the Rift.": "grief",
      "This spring, somebody unlocked the Black Gate.": "dread",
      "We did not know who.": "calm",
      "Oswin, the master of our Order, turned the light of all his towers on it and drove it back, until the gap was only as wide as a cart.": "passion",
      "Then the ground gave way, and he fell through.": "grief",
      "His lantern was still lit.": "hope",
      "Six armies came out through the gap, each led by a grey-eyed champion we called a Herald.": "dread",
      "I am Ysolde, Queen of Solenne.": "pride",
      "You are a Spirewright, the last of Oswin's apprentices.": "warm",
      "You build the towers.": "calm",
      "We take the lands back one at a time.": "passion",
      "Hold the road to each town.": "fierce",
      "Kill its Herald.": "fierce",
      "Free its Warden.": "passion",
      "Each Herald went home, to the land they were born in.": "dread",
      "A Warden lets its own people come close.": "grief",
      "There each Herald whispered to its Warden until the Warden went mad.": "dread",
      "A mad Warden turns its own element on its own people.": "dread",
      "The volcano poured out its fire.": "dread",
      "The forest strangled its towns.": "dread",
      "And the Herald raised an army out of the land itself.": "cold"
    },
    "assault_intro": {
      "A road is cut into the wall of the Rift.": "calm",
      "It took us a day to walk down it.": "weary",
      "At the bottom we went through the gap in the Black Gate one at a time, the way his armies had come out.": "dread",
      "Behind the Gate is the Hollow, a cavern under the world so big its roof is lost in the dark.": "awe",
      "The only light is grey fire.": "dread",
      "A day's march in stood his fortress, Nhal Vorath, built from the ruins of his old city, which sank with him.": "calm",
      "His army was still too big to storm.": "calm",
      "So we dug in in front of his walls, built our towers, and let it come to us.": "pride",
      "You built your city on my city, and you lock my door with my own crown.": "bitter",
      "Come in, then.": "menace",
      "For once we're not holding a road, Spirewright.": "wry",
      "We're on his.": "fierce"
    },
    "capital_prelude": {
      "...There's a light on the east road.": "whisper",
      "Does nobody else see it?": "hope",
      "Every land we had freed sent its fighters to Solenne: Emberfolk smiths, Galeborn riders, Deepwood archers, Tidefolk, Stoneborn and Veilwalkers.": "pride",
      "Cassivane came for the Heartstone himself.": "dread",
      "He had fused the pieces of the Sunstone into his own body.": "calm",
      "We called what he had become the Sundered Heart.": "dread",
      "If he takes the Heartstone, the Gate opens all the way and Vael-Orrun walks out.": "calm",
      "So he does not take it.": "cold",
      "Hold this wall.": "command"
    },
    "convergence_intro": {
      "With all six Wardens awake, their oath held Vael-Orrun again, and the gap in the Gate could get no wider.": "hope",
      "Only the whole Heartstone could break the oath now.": "dread",
      "So everything he had left came out of the Rift at once and marched west for Solenne, with Cassivane at its head.": "dread",
      "We raced it home.": "passion",
      "The Wardens walked with us.": "awe",
      "Queen of Solenne.": "cold",
      "When this is over, I will tell you what we did at Vael.": "grief",
      "Not before.": "cold",
      "Cassivane's army was camped at Crossmere, the town where every road on the Ring meets, a day east of Solenne.": "calm",
      "We had to go through him.": "passion"
    },
    "crossroads": {
      "We held Crossmere.": "pride",
      "Cassivane fought like the hero he used to be, then pulled back with what was left of his army.": "bitter",
      "Yes.": "cold",
      "I opened the Gate.": "weary",
      "He had my daughter.": "grief",
      "He gave her back to me empty.": "bitter",
      "She will be whole when he is free.": "passion",
      "He left her behind.": "bitter",
      "In the cage was Ilyra, six years gone.": "awe",
      "She was alive, but she did not know her own name.": "grief",
      "Corvin sat with her all night.": "tender",
      "By morning she knew his name.": "hope",
      "By the next, she knew her own.": "warm",
      "Behind the Gate I heard two voices.": "hollow",
      "One of them wept.": "dread",
      "The other never did.": "dread",
      "My father only ever heard the first.": "grief",
      "Let me help you stop him.": "passion"
